    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really good point about the legislative stuff. i feel like a lot of people today try to argue that unions actually hurt the economy or make things less efficient, but it seems like they're just making excuses to protect high-level profits. do you think those criticisms are actually valid, or are they just biased arguments used to undermine worker progress?",
