      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even when unions are essential for democracy, valid criticisms exist regarding the potential rigification of certain industries or the political influence they can exert over politicians. One specific downside involves \"double dissent,\" where the perceived need to outperform a union can lead some companies to cut the necessary wages of non-union workers, thereby harming overall economic health.\n\nHowever, these challenges are often seen as growing pains of the system rather than a fundamental flaw that negates their democratic value. Ultimately, the tradeoff is usually between short-term economic distortion and the long-term fair distribution of political power that unions secure for the populace.",
